target
artifacts
coverage
# The curated seed corpus under corpus/<target>/ *is* tracked — it's the real, valid protocol
# data fuzzing needs to be worth anything. What's ignored is what a real local fuzzing run adds on
# top of it: libFuzzer names newly-discovered inputs by content hash. Matching "starts with a hex
# digit" was tried first and was wrong — plenty of real words (checkerboard, framed_and_liquid)
# start with a-f too. Naming every curated seed with an unambiguous `seed_`/`regression_` prefix
# and ignoring everything else in a target's corpus directory has no such false-positive risk.
corpus/*/*
!corpus/*/seed_*
!corpus/*/regression_*
